{
  "kanji": "魚",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 魚\ntitle: fish\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, pictograph, starter]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 魚\nradicalNumber: 195\nonyomi: [ギョ]\nkunyomi: [うお, さかな, -ざかな]\ndistractors: [田, 食, 犬]\n---\n\n# 魚 — fish\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 魚 (no. 195) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n魚 is a pictograph of a fish: the head at the top, the body (田-like) in the middle and the tail at the bottom. In the old shapes the tail was drawn as a fan, and in modern print it became four dots (灬).\nThe 田 in the middle is a convenient mnemonic for a scaly body, not the kanji 田 (field) in meaning.\nAs a radical it shows up in many fish names: 鯉, 鮪, 鯛 and so on.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ギョ | on | [金魚](../words/金魚.md) きんぎょ, 人魚 にんぎょ, 魚類 ぎょるい, 熱帯魚 ねったいぎょ |\n| さかな | kun | [魚](../words/魚.md) さかな, 焼き魚 やきざかな |\n| うお | kun | 魚市場 うおいちば, 魚座 うおざ (the constellation Pisces) |\n| -ざかな | kun | 小魚 こざかな (voiced form in compounds) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [魚](../words/魚.md) さかな — fish\n- [金魚](../words/金魚.md) きんぎょ — goldfish\n\n## Notes\n\nさかな originally meant the food that goes with sake (酒 + 菜); the word later turned into \"fish\". This is the widely cited explanation.\nDo not confuse 魚 with 鳥 (とり, bird), which has a similar frame.\n",
